    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35601" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνθνήσκω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>die in,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χθονὸς . . τοσοῦτον, [ὥστε] ἐνθανεῖν
					μόνον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OC</u>
					790
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				869
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σῇ χερί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Heracl.</u>
					560
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of the hand,
				<i>grow rigid</i> or <i>torpid in,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Hec.</u>
					246
				</span></i>
			.—Dub. in Prose, <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				16.15
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐναπο-</span> Markland), <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.357d
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκθ-</span> Reiske).</div>
